  "Number": 1,
  "Question": "What is the value of \\(2 - (-2)^{-2}?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-2\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{16}\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac{7}{4}\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac{9}{4}\\)",
    "E": "\\(6\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "For a nonzero base, a negative exponent means taking the reciprocal of the corresponding positive power. Thus\n\\[\n(-2)^{-2}=\\frac{1}{(-2)^2}=\\frac14.\n\\]\nEvaluate this power before subtracting:\n\\[\n2-(-2)^{-2}=2-\\frac14=\\boxed{\\frac74},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
